Z||000000||AL||01-28-2001||09:21 PM||||<BR>well i replaced the fuel pump on this baby and it only cost me 32 bucks with my uncles discount he gets at autozone,i've noticed that with the new ac delco fuel pump, i don't get that old wining noise that i get from my gt's fuel pump,so i will probably change my gt's fuel pump soon.well i started the indy and this little motor works great,my biggest problem was bleeding the clutch or slave to ingage, and it looks like it does, but i need to get the steel pedal for it so it can change gears better,but all in all, it's all comming together,after i change the pedal, next stop will be the paint shop.well that's it for now, once i get it running right i will post more pics for you guys & and gals<B>AL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">   <BR>86gt 84indy<P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 01-28-2001).]||||reg||14
